        "hypothesis": "A conservative size-scaled direct-recurrence horizon should avoid dense matrix exponentiation for more short-to-moderate distances, while the tiled transposed matrix fallback retains coverage for larger distances. Delaying matrix setup until fallback avoids unnecessary work on the direct path.",
        "id": "d4fd3053320045be",
